amendmentsChecked.detail:
backend/libs/core/src/modules/receivables/ageing-rebuild.ts, one tenantStorage.run(ctx, () => withTenant(db, ctx, tx => …)) per page, in this order:
1. retailerIdPage (no lock);
2. `select retailer_id from retailer_outstanding_summary where tenant_id = … and retailer_id in (idList) order by retailer_id for update`;
3. rebuildAgeingPage(tx, asOf, ids).

Nothing else is locked. rebuildAgeingPage only reads bills and credit and upserts summary and snapshot rows (outstanding.ts:321-331, :266-292, :384-429).

The owner's rebuildAgeing also locks summary rows in ascending retailer_id order: pages come ordered by id, computeOutstanding keeps that order in its Map, and the upsert VALUES follow it. So the two rebuild paths cannot deadlock each other.

